    {
      "id": "40733774",
      "title": "Divide and Conquer",
      "lectureOrder": 484,
      "videoOrder": 483,
      "sourceHash": "87214f7f8c3c0a9a64ac82658f00cfeb060f1c5f6263eafcb3c788ee157c311f",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.15,
          "end": 2.04,
          "en": "-: In this video, we'll talk about divide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.57,
          "en": "and conquer technique.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 3.57,
          "end": 5.58,
          "en": "The thing is, in the upcoming algorithms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 5.58,
          "end": 6.69,
          "en": "which you're going to learn,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 6.69,
          "end": 8.46,
          "en": "we are going to use this technique.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 8.46,
          "end": 11.7,
          "en": "So it makes sense to talk about this technique separately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 11.7,
          "end": 14.07,
          "en": "The thing is, when you talk about any algorithm,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 14.07,
          "end": 15.72,
          "en": "what we are trying to do is we are trying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 15.72,
          "end": 17.22,
          "en": "to solve a particular problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 17.22,
          "end": 19.32,
          "en": "Now, of course, when you learn a particular algorithm,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 19.32,
          "end": 21.84,
          "en": "we normally work with limited set of values, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 21.84,
          "end": 25.11,
          "en": "Let's say five values, six values, or maybe 10 values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 25.11,
          "end": 27.51,
          "en": "But still, these are small numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 27.51,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "What if you are working with huge amount of data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 31.56,
          "en": "Now, that's where one of the issue which comes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 31.56,
          "end": 33.6,
          "en": "which is your time complexity, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 33.6,
          "end": 35.7,
          "en": "So basically whatever algorithm we are learning,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 38.52,
          "en": "we are trying to understand which algorithm goes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 38.52,
          "end": 40.17,
          "en": "for what time complexity?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 40.17,
          "end": 41.94,
          "en": "So basically when we talk about bubble sort,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 41.94,
          "end": 43.05,
          "en": "when you talk about selection sort,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 43.05,
          "end": 46.5,
          "en": "they have a different time complexity which is much higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 46.5,
          "end": 48.42,
          "en": "and on the other hand, when you talk about quick sort,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 48.42,
          "end": 50.19,
          "en": "it is much more time efficient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 50.19,
          "end": 51.33,
          "en": "So how does that really work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 51.33,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "So what they do is they basically take a big task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "now, it can be for small numbers as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 57.75,
          "en": "you take a task, you take a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 57.75,
          "end": 59.97,
          "en": "and you try to find a solution of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 59.97,
          "end": 61.62,
          "en": "Of course, every algorithm does that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 61.62,
          "end": 65.22,
          "en": "So we have a problem, and we find a solution for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 65.22,
          "end": 67.86,
          "en": "Now, in divide and conquer, as a name suggests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 67.86,
          "end": 71.55,
          "en": "what you do is you divide first, and then you conquer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 71.55,
          "end": 72.72,
          "en": "and then you combine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 72.72,
          "end": 76.08,
          "en": "Now what it means, let's say we have a big problem called P.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 76.08,
          "end": 77.88,
          "en": "Now what you will do is you will break it down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 77.88,
          "end": 79.71000000000001,
          "en": "into subsections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 79.71000000000001,
          "end": 81.84,
          "en": "So you will say P1, P2, and list goes on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 81.84,
          "end": 82.98,
          "en": "And then what you will do is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 82.98,
          "end": 86.94,
          "en": "you will apply the algorithm on each subsection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 86.94,
          "end": 89.28,
          "en": "so on P1, P2, P3,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 89.28,
          "end": 91.5,
          "en": "and then what you will get is a solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 91.5,
          "end": 92.94,
          "en": "for that particular subproblem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 92.94,
          "end": 95.43,
          "en": "So by doing this, you are trying to solve a big problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 95.43,
          "end": 97.47,
          "en": "by breaking it down into small parts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 97.47,
          "end": 100.68,
          "en": "And then, what you will do is you will simply solve it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 100.68,
          "end": 102.45,
          "en": "each subproblem, and then you will merge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 102.45,
          "end": 103.53,
          "en": "you will combine them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 103.53,
          "end": 105.9,
          "en": "and that's where you will get a solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 105.9,
          "end": 108.53999999999999,
          "en": "or a big solution for the big problem, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 108.53999999999999,
          "end": 111.72,
          "en": "Now, what if the subsection itself is huge?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 111.72,
          "end": 113.787,
          "en": "So let's say when you say P, that's a big problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 113.787,
          "end": 116.82,
          "en": "P1, P2, what if even they are huge?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 116.82,
          "end": 117.69,
          "en": "Now, in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 117.69,
          "end": 120.03,
          "en": "what you will do is you will again divide them to sub parts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 120.03,
          "end": 122.82,
          "en": "Something like P11 and P21,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 122.82,
          "end": 124.77,
          "en": "or maybe you can have P1 goes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 127.5,
          "en": "for P11, P12, so those are the subproblems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 127.5,
          "end": 129.39,
          "en": "and then you try to solve them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 129.39,
          "end": 131.34,
          "en": "so that it will be easier to solve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 131.34,
          "end": 133.17,
          "en": "Now that's what we call divide.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 133.17,
          "end": 135.45,
          "en": "And of course, when you divide and conquer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 135.45,
          "end": 136.74,
          "en": "don't forget to combine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 136.74,
          "end": 138.06,
          "en": "And we have to also make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 138.06,
          "end": 139.65,
          "en": "that after dividing this problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 139.65,
          "end": 141.57,
          "en": "after solving them, when you combine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 141.57,
          "end": 143.49,
          "en": "you get a desired result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 143.49,
          "end": 146.16,
          "en": "Maybe when you solve a particular problem, the subsection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 146.16,
          "end": 146.993,
          "en": "they are working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 146.993,
          "end": 149.94,
          "en": "You got the output, which is desired for subproblem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 149.94,
          "end": 151.17000000000002,
          "en": "but what about when you combine it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 151.17000000000002,
          "end": 152.46,
          "en": "you got some different answer?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 153.84,
          "en": "Even that will not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 153.84,
          "end": 156.66,
          "en": "So you have to make sure that when you combine the work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 156.66,
          "end": 158.46,
          "en": "you will get your desired results.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 158.46,
          "end": 160.26,
          "en": "Now, most of the people have this confusion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 160.26,
          "end": 161.94,
          "en": "when you talk about divide and conquer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 161.94,
          "end": 164.19,
          "en": "that we can divide the task the way we want, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 164.19,
          "end": 165.023,
          "en": "No.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 165.023,
          "end": 166.89,
          "en": "So basically, whatever algorithm you're going to apply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 166.89,
          "end": 168.03,
          "en": "on the big problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 168.03,
          "end": 171.27,
          "en": "the same algorithm should work on the each subsection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 171.27,
          "end": 172.82999999999998,
          "en": "So let's say an example, let's say if I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 172.82999999999998,
          "end": 174.15,
          "en": "to paint the entire house,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 174.15,
          "end": 175.53,
          "en": "let's say we have four rooms there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 175.53,
          "end": 178.23,
          "en": "and that I want to paint each room.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 178.23,
          "end": 180.96,
          "en": "So basically, painting the entire house is a big problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 180.96,
          "end": 183.12,
          "en": "So what you will do is you will divide the task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 183.12,
          "end": 185.73,
          "en": "Now, if you're thinking, dividing tasks simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 185.73,
          "end": 188.4,
          "en": "that someone will buy the paint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 188.4,
          "end": 192.48,
          "en": "someone will apply the paint, someone will clean the floors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 192.48,
          "end": 194.13,
          "en": "no, that's not the task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 194.13,
          "end": 195.99,
          "en": "What we can do is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 195.99,
          "end": 198.66,
          "en": "instead of painting the entire house, instead of,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 198.66,
          "end": 200.7,
          "en": "I mean of course you have to paint the entire house,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 200.7,
          "end": 201.75,
          "en": "but you can divide the problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 201.75,
          "end": 203.07,
          "en": "you can say, okay, we have full house,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 203.07,
          "end": 206.55,
          "en": "let's divide it, the four rooms into four separate parts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 206.55,
          "end": 207.48,
          "en": "paint each room.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 207.48,
          "end": 210.12,
          "en": "Of course, in each room you will buy the paint,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 210.12,
          "end": 212.52,
          "en": "you will apply the paint, you will clean the floor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 212.52,
          "end": 214.62,
          "en": "I only remember those three steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 214.62,
          "end": 216.84,
          "en": "So basically, you will do it for each room.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 216.84,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "So what you have done is you have divided the big problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 221.57999999999998,
          "en": "solved it, and then you combine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 221.57999999999998,
          "end": 223.86,
          "en": "Of course, you have to also combine those four rooms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 223.86,
          "end": 225.42000000000002,
          "en": "to get a house, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 225.42000000000002,
          "end": 227.923,
          "en": "That's what divide and conquer is.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
